 - **Unchanged retail shoe exports preserve their palette and distance images (maumau78).** "this texture was just exported then imported into another slot but still glitched in-game" now has a regression test through Export PNG and the package compiler. Original-size copies preserve the retail palette and all mip bytes; the same-slot result is the original span, and a compatible other slot reuses its shared image without growing memory. An incompatible slot must fit the exact artwork or refuse. Half or quarter size deliberately removes detail, new art can merge colours to fit P8 or the compressed slot, and palette-only mode keeps the retail shape; the import summary explains these losses. The reported in-game smear remains unwitnessed after this change.
